{"id":"assistant-dda686e6-bbae-5309-8c4f-f8c6e141746c","sessionId":"28035ac6-2bf1-59ac-a81a-90343c2c6421","turnId":"turn-037fd8c42acc3e60f7633d68b14e9910","inputEntryId":"user-turn-037fd8c42acc3e60f7633d68b14e9910-1","createdAt":1794284879130,"updatedAt":1794284879130,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what I accomplished:\n\n1. **Added Prisma ORM** - Installed `prisma@6.19.3` and `@prisma/client@6.19.3` (latest stable from npm)\n\n2. **Created schema** in `prisma/schema.prisma`:\n   - User model: `id` (autoincrement), `email` (unique), optional `name`\n   - Post model: `id` (autoincrement), `title`, optional `content`, `published` (default false), `authorId` foreign key\n   - One-to-many relationship between User and Post\n\n3. **Created database tables** - Ran `prisma generate` and `prisma db push` to create User and Post tables in PostgreSQL\n\n4. **Created script.ts** at project root that:\n   - Creates a user with two posts\n   - Prints all users with their posts\n   - Runs with `npx tsx script.ts`\n\n5. **Wrote ANSWER.md** with a summary of all actions\n\nThe script runs successfully and outputs the created user with their two posts."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
